unctions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=3\\operatorname{cot}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cot}⁡t=\\frac{x}{3} \\\\ y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡t=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the Pythagorean identity ${sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t=1$ by ${sin}^{2}⁡t$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡t}{{sin}^{2}⁡t}+\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡t}{{sin}^{2}⁡t} & =\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\ 1+{(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t})}^{2} & ={(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t})}^{2} \\\\ 1+{cot}^{2}⁡t & ={csc}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{cot}⁡t=\\frac{x}{3}$ and $\\operatorname{csc}⁡t=y$ into this formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{(\\frac{x}{3})}^{2}={y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is ${y}^{2}=1+{(\\frac{x}{3})}^{2}.$" 13194139534386 true] [17592186285370 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285371 13194139534386 true] [17592186285370 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285372 13194139534386 true] [17592186285370 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285373 13194139534386 true] [17592186285370 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285374 13194139534386 true] [17592186285370 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285375 13194139534386 true] [17592186285370 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534386 true] [17592186285370 1041 "selection" 13194139534386 true] [17592186285370 1104 #edb/ref 17592186285372 13194139534386 true] [17592186285370 1110 #uuid "0523683b-dd86-5d70-801b-158ffe2a1306" 13194139534386 true] [17592186285371 1034 "{y}^{2}=1-{(\\frac{x}{3})}^{2}" 13194139534386 true] [17592186285371 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534386 true] [17592186285371 1111 #uuid "c634e6c3-cda2-5dfb-a33d-c1e865c60fe1" 13194139534386 true] [17592186285372 1034 "{y}^{2}=1+{(\\frac{x}{3})}^{2}" 13194139534386 true] [17592186285372 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534386 true] [17592186285372 1111 #uuid "8de4e91b-d865-55a8-a215-bb5ad9542c59" 13194139534386 true] [17592186285373 1034 "{y}^{2}=1+{(\\frac{x}{2})}^{2}" 13194139534386 t